File: src/common/update.rs, Lines: 803-912

```rust
for operation in operations {
    let current_update_result = match operation {
        UpdateOperation::Upsert(operation) => {
            let (result, usage) = do_upsert_points(
                toc_provider.clone(),
                collection_name.clone(),
                operation.upsert,
                internal_params,
                params,
                auth.clone(),
                inference_params.clone(),
                hw_measurement_acc.clone(),
            )
            .await?;  // <-- Short-circuits on error, returns immediately

            inference_usage.merge_opt(usage);
            result
        }
        // ... other operation types with same .await? pattern
    };

    results.push(current_update_result);
}
```

Key observation: The `.await?` operator in the for loop causes immediate return on first error. No rollback mechanism exists. No operations are applied before validation, so the batch fails atomically (with zero side effects), which is correct fail-fast behavior.
